{{ macros.section(2, "Project Stats", id="project-statistics") }}

{# Single source of truth: the `stats` plugin (.automation.cmk, loaded by the
   project Makefile) computes every figure below, the compiler size/partition
   metrics, the test / target / suite counts, and the coverage summary, and emits
   one JSON object.  The render just projects it, so this page and the `make stats`
   entrypoint can never drift.  `-s` silences make; the target's `log` banner
   goes to stderr, so stdout is pure JSON.

   The `stats` target builds its JSON with `jb` (json.bash), but the docs render
   image ships no `jb` (and no docker for the containerized fallback), so bootstrap a
   native json.bash into the PATH if it is missing, quiet, and only fetched once per
   render, so `${jb}` resolves via `which jb` instead of failing to empty output. -#}
{% set s   = bash('make -s stats', load_json=True) -%}
{% set cov = s.get('target_coverage') or {} -%}

| Statistic | Value | What it measures |
|-----------|-------|------------------|
| `total_sloc` | `{{ s.get('total_sloc', 'n/a') }}` | source lines of code[^sloc] in `compose.mk`, minus blank / comment / `@#` docstring lines (= compiler + core) |
| `compiler_sloc` | `{{ s.get('compiler_sloc', 'n/a') }}` | non-blank / non-comment lines inside the core's `define .awk.*` compiler blocks (see `lang.comp.stats`) |
| `core_sloc` | `{{ s.get('core_sloc', 'n/a') }}` | total SLOC minus the compiler `.awk.*` blocks (= seed + hosted) |
| `hosted_sloc` | `{{ s.get('hosted_sloc', 'n/a') }}` | SLOC in the self-hosted `define __hosted__` partition |
| `seed_sloc` | `{{ s.get('seed_sloc', 'n/a') }}` | core SLOC minus the hosted partition (the hand-written seed) |
| `compiler_ratio` | `{{ s.get('compiler_ratio', 'n/a') }}` | non-comment core source characters per non-comment awk character |
| `test_count` | `{{ s.get('test_count', 'n/a') }}` | `def test_*` functions across every suite |
| `tests_sloc` | `{{ s.get('tests_sloc', 'n/a') }}` | source lines of code[^sloc] across the test suite, minus blank / comment lines |
| `suite_list` | the pytest suite markers | `{{ s.get('suite_list', 'n/a') }}` |
| `target_count` | `{{ s.get('target_count', 'n/a') }}` | public targets in core, via the canonical parser |
| `target_coverage` | `{{ cov.get('covered', 'n/a') }} / {{ cov.get('denominator', 'n/a') }}` ({{ cov.get('percent', 'n/a') }}%) | core targets exercised by the suite, from the coverage summary |

